<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alfred Sharpe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1853–1935</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alfred Sharpe was a British lawyer, hunter and colonial administrator who became commissioner of the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-africa">Central Africa</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> in 1896 and its first governor when it was renamed Nyasaland in 1907, serving until 1910. He extended British control over the territory west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-malawi">Lake Malawi</a> through treaties and military campaigns.</p></div>
